    backlog:hasTestSpec "08-tooling/ch05-deck/build_v1_0_0.sh built deck 1.0.0 as a lecture from the start - 37 slides, a talk track in every slide's notes, click-by-click builds, a debugger simulator, a logging-level matrix and an exception climb drawn as native shapes from executed specifications - and ran its three checks under Python 3.14.4: deck_check_v1_0_1.py re-ran 8 expressions, program_check_v1_0_0.py re-executed 18 program runs, visual_check_v1_1_0.py re-checked 103 visual values against specifications regenerated by running visuals_make_v1_0_0.py - 0 mismatches. Four fixtures refused, each naming what it broke: an expression on slide 11 (issubclass(AssertionError, Exception) shown as False), a program transcript (the buggy adding program), a debugger variable on slide 28 (x = 6 shown for x = 5) and a logging-matrix cell on slide 16 (hidden shown for shown); the visual check also refuses a stale fixture of its own inputs. Rendered and inspected; layout overflows and overlaps fixed before closing. The first run of the expression check used the system Python 3.11 and refused a correct slide (finding Finding_Ch05DeckCheckInterpreter); the build now runs every check under the interpreter the course teaches." ; backlog:hasVerificationMethod "Gates run over the artefacts as published in the release carrying 03-materials/ch05/SEN0414_Ch05_Debugging_3e_v1_0_0.pptx (sen0414-v2.31.0)." ;
